Hi gang!  Professor Tim here.  Ready to walk you through all the steps of building your own puzzle.  Just follow my directions in these handy little Help Windows.  Click on "continue" whenever you're ready to go on.  Click on "go back" if you change your mind about the last thing you did.  Or click on "Bye!" if you want to leave this Walk-Through.
Hey there.  Professor Tim at your service! I'll walk you through the whole process of building your own puzzle.  Anytime you don't know what to do next, just click on me (on the control panel to the left), and I'll come help you out.
The first thing you want to do is take some parts out of the Parts Bin on the right and put them on the screen.  See what kind of incredible machines you can build out of all those gadgets and gizmos.  Anytime you don't know what to do next, just click on my face (on the control panel to the left) and I'll come help you out.
Make sure you've got all the parts you want on the screen.  When you're done, click on me again.
Before we can go any further, you'll have to put at least five parts on the screen.
Excellent!  You've got some great looking stuff going on!  If you're totally finished putting parts on the screen, click on "continue."  If you want to do more work on your machine, choose "go back."  If you want to leave this Walk-Through, click on "Bye!"
Now let's select some music to go with your puzzle.
Sounds like you've already picked out some tunes to go with your puzzle.  But you can make changes if you want.  Choose "continue" to bring up the Music Menu, then make your music changes or choose "done."
Check out the tune that's playing right now.  If this is the music you want to go with your puzzle choose "continue."  If it's not, click on "go back" to bring up the Music Menu.
Your puzzle will need a goal, and a title.  First let's write a goal (for example:  "Pop the balloon").  Just type one into the white box at the bottom of the puzzle screen, then hit "Enter" (or "Return") on your keyboard.
You've already given your puzzle a goal.  But you can change it if you want.  Choose "continue," then type your changes into the white box below.  When you're finished, click anywhere on the screen.
Oops. . .  You can't have an empty Goal Window.  You'll have to type something in.
If your goal says exactly what you want it to, click on "continue."  If you want to make changes, choose "go back."
Now your puzzle needs a name.  This name will appear in the Homemade Puzzles file once you've saved your puzzle.  Then players will be able to load your puzzle and play it!
DELETE TEXT:  Looks like you've already written a name for your puzzle.  But you can change it if you want to.  Choose "continue" to bring up the Puzzle Name window.  Then you can type in a new name, or just choose "done" if you're satisfied.
You didn't give your puzzle a name.  You'll have to type something in.
If this is the name you want for your puzzle, click on "continue."  If not, choose "go back" to make changes.
All right!  Now let's add some hints!  You can put a hint any place you think players might need a little help.
DELETE TEXT:  Ah!  I see you've got some hints in your puzzle already.  But you can make changes or add new ones if you want.  Click on "continue" to bring up the Hints window.  Then you can either change your hints or choose "done."
If you're sure you don't want to add any hints, click on "continue."  If you DO want to add hints, choose "go back."
If you're all done working on hints, click on "continue."  If you want to add or change hints, choose "go back."
Looking great so far!  Now it's time to program a solution for your puzzle.  You can do this by clicking on any of the parts that solve your puzzle, then choosing the checkered flag.
Excellent!  You've already programmed a solution into your puzzle!  If you aren't satisfied with it, go ahead and change it.  You can program a solution by clicking on any of the parts that solve your puzzle, then choosing the checkered flag.
You haven't programmed a solution for your puzzle.  If you're sure you don't want one, click on "continue."  If you DO want a solution, choose "go back."  You can program a solution by clicking on any of the parts that solve your puzzle, then choosing the checkered flag.
If you're happy with your puzzle solution click on "continue."  If you want to make changes, choose "go back."
Now you need to lock down the parts in your puzzle.  All the unlocked parts will go into the parts bin when the puzzle is played.  Click on "continue" to lock all parts.
I see you've already locked down some of the parts in your puzzle.  Now you need to lock down the rest of them.  Click on "continue" to lock all parts.
Great!  All your parts are locked down.  Now unlock all the parts you want to show up in the parts bin when the puzzle is played.  Click on the padlock icon for each part you want to unlock.  Come get me again when you're finished.
If you have unlocked all the parts you want to appear in the parts bin, click on "continue."  If you want to unlock some more parts, choose "go back."
Now for the finishing touches!  Time to save your puzzle.  Click on Continue and I will go save it.
Sorry... your puzzle wasn't successfully saved.  This might be because you're trying to save to a write-protected disk, or you're on a network with limited space, or your computer has a configuration problem.  If you want to give it another try, click on "continue."
All right!!!  Your puzzle has been saved!  If you decide you want to work on it again sometime, you'll have to go to the Workshop, choose "Load a new puzzle."  Then click on "Homemade Puzzles" and choose your puzzle name from the list.
Excellent puzzle building!  Looks like we're all done for now.  Come back for another Walk-Through anytime you need a quick review!
